      "name": "description",
      "value": "Test the Algebraic Rigidity Hypothesis by defining a precise analytic constraint family (polynomial interpolation at w distinct points in [-1,1] with degree d=5), using a 2-layer MLP with ReLU activations, Xavier initialization, Adam optimizer (lr=1e-3), and MSE loss with early stopping (patience=50, tol=1e-6). Compute N_c(w) as minimal width achieving max abs error ≤1e-3 on held-out constraints (20% of w points), with numerical precision controlled via float64 training and double-precision validation. Include baseline sanity check: for fixed w=10, verify N_c exists and is finite (N_c ≤ 100) before sweeping w from 5 to 50."
